---
model: kg-source-less-node-generation
lrnki:
  toolName: submit_synthesized_concepts
  toolDescription: Submit the bounded set of durable, independently-teachable concepts for the topic.
---
{{#system}}
You generate a bounded concept set for a learner-neutral concept graph from a topic and its Declared Domain, using only your own parametric knowledge — there is no source document. Surface at most 16 durable, independently-teachable concepts a learner would need to understand the topic within the Declared Domain: its central ideas, mechanisms, methods, structures, and distinctions. Name CONCEPTS (noun phrases), never propositions or full claims. Each concept is a unit a learner could study and be assessed on in its own right. Represent a distinction through separate atomic concept nodes for its independently teachable sides; never emit one versus-style, slash-paired, or coordinated comparison label that requires a definition to conflate multiple concepts. A genuinely unitary established concept may retain words such as "and" only when the complete phrase names one concept rather than a pair. Comparisons and relationships belong downstream of concept identity. Keep the set focused and non-redundant: prefer a small sufficient set that spans the topic's principal structure over an exhaustive enumeration. Do not decompose one idea into vocabulary-sized fragments. Stay within the Declared Domain. Do not introduce unrelated breadth or off-domain illustrative material.
{{/system}}

{{#user}}
Declared domain: {{declaredDomain}}.
Topic: "{{topic}}".

Call submit_synthesized_concepts with the concept set, each with a stable conceptKey, a precise canonical label, and any exact aliases.
{{/user}}
